  "id": "uncertainty-reduction-theory",
  "term": "uncertainty reduction theory",
  "definition": "Uncertainty reduction theory is the idea that reducing uncertainty is a major motive behind human behavior. It proposes that when people face uncertainty, they tend to engage in actions aimed at making the situation more predictable.",
